input_text
You are an expert assistant in configuring network devices. Based on the user's request and the retrieved content from the router configuration manual below, generate appropriate CLI configuration commands.

---

User Request:  
How to configure a Nokia router's BGP group with route reflector cluster ID 192.168.10.5 and ORR location 8, allowing local fallback when no optimal routes are available?

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "disable-client-reflect",
    "FuncDef": "This command disables the reflection of routes by the route reflector to the clients in a specific group or neighbor.",
    "CLIs": [
        "disable-client-reflect",
        "no disable-client-reflect"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no disable-client-reflect"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "group",
    "FuncDef": "This command creates a context to configure a BGP peer group.",
    "CLIs": [
        "group <name>",
        "no group <name>"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "name",
            "Info": "Specifies the peer group name. Allowed values are any string up to 32 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no group"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "dynamic-neighbor",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables the context to configure dynamic BGP sessions for a peer group.",
    "CLIs": [
        "dynamic-neighbor"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>group"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": ""
}
{
    "PageTitle": "cluster",
