---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to enable BGP rapid updates for EVPN address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
{
  "commands": [
    "config>router>bgp>family evpn",
    "config>router>bgp>error-handling"
  ]
}
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
rapid-update [ l2-vpn ] [ mvpn-ipv4 ] [ mvpn-ipv6 ] [ mdt-safi ] [ evpn ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ] [ vpn-ipv4 ] [ vpn-ipv6 ] [ mcast-vpn-ipv4 ] [ mcast-vpn-ipv6 ]
no rapid-update
FuncDef:
This command enables and disables BGP rapid update for specified address families.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'l2-vpn', 'Info': 'Specifies the BGP rapid update for the 12-byte Virtual Switch Instance identifier (VSI-ID) value consisting of the 8-byte route distinguisher (RD) followed by a 4-byte value.'}
{'Parameters': 'mvpn-ipv4', 'Info': 'Specifies BGP rapid update for the mvpn-ipv4 address family. The mvpn-pv4 address is a variable size value consisting of the 1-byte route type, 1-byte length and variable size that is route type specific. Route type defines encoding for the route type specific field. Length indicates the length in octets of the route type specific field.'}
{'Parameters': 'mdt-safi', 'Info': 'Specifies BGP rapid update for the mdt-safi address family. The address is a 16-byte value consisting of 12-byte route distinguisher (RD) followed by a 4-byte group address.'}
