You are an expert assistant in configuring network devices. Based on the user's request and the retrieved content from the router configuration manual below, generate appropriate CLI configuration commands.

---

User Request:  
How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 diverse VPN-IPv4 paths to BGP peers while disabling the receive capability?

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "disable-client-reflect",
    "FuncDef": "This command disables the reflection of routes by the route reflector to the clients in a specific group or neighbor.",
    "CLIs": [
        "disable-client-reflect",
        "no disable-client-reflect"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no disable-client-reflect"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "shutdown",
    "FuncDef": "This command administratively disables an entity. When disabled, an entity does not change, reset, or remove any configuration settings or statistics.",
    "CLIs": [
        "shutdown",
        "no shutdown"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor",
        "config>router>bgp>monitor",
        "config>bmp",
        "config>bmp>station",
        "config>bmp>station>connection>tcp-keepalive",
        "config>router>bgp>monitor",
        "config>router>bgp>group>monitor",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>monitor",
        "config>service>vprn>bgp>monitor",
